    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include \\\"knn.h\\\"\\n#include <arm_neon.h>\\n\\n// Max-heap node structure\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float dist;\\n    char label;\\n} HeapNode;\\n\\nstatic inline void heap_swap(HeapNode *a, HeapNode *b) {\\n    HeapNode t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t;\\n}\\n\\n// Insert a single (dist,label) into the max-heap of size k.\\nstatic inline void heap_insert_or_replace(float d, char label,\\n                                          HeapNode *heap, int *heap_size_ptr, int k) {\\n    int heap_size = *heap_size_ptr;\\n    if (heap_size < k) {\\n        // Insert into heap\\n        heap_size++;\\n        int idx = heap_size;\\n        heap[idx].dist = d;\\n        heap[idx].label = label;\\n        while (idx > 1 && heap[idx >> 1].dist < heap[idx].dist) {\\n            heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[idx >> 1]);\\n            idx >>= 1;\\n        }\\n    } else if (d < heap[1].dist) {\\n        // Replace root\\n        heap[1].dist = d;\\n        heap[1].label = label;\\n        int idx = 1;\\n        while (1) {\\n            int largest = idx;\\n            int left = idx << 1;\\n            int right = (idx << 1) + 1;\\n            if (left <= heap_size && heap[left].dist > heap[largest].dist)\\n                largest = left;\\n            if (right <= heap_size && heap[right].dist > heap[largest].dist)\\n                largest = right;\\n            if (largest != idx) {\\n                heap_swap(&heap[idx], &heap[largest]);\\n                idx = largest;\\n            } else break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    *heap_size_ptr = heap_size;\\n}\\n\\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\\n    // Allocate labels array (initialized with -1 sentinel)\\n    char *labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) labels[i] = -1;\\n\\n    // Max-heap of size k+1 (index 1..k)\\n    HeapNode *heap = (HeapNode *) malloc(sizeof(HeapNode) * (k + 1));\\n    int heap_size = 0;\\n\\n    // Hoist NEON vector constants for the target point (invariant across all groups)\\n    float32x4_t tx_vec = vdupq_n_f32(to_evaluate.x);\\n    float32x4_t ty_vec = vdupq_n_f32(to_evaluate.y);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        Group g = groups[i];\\n        // Use restrict and assume_aligned hints to help vectorization\\n        float *restrict xs = __builtin_assume_aligned(g.xs, 16);\\n        float *restrict ys = __builtin_assume_aligned(g.ys, 16);\\n        int len = g.length;\\n        char label = g.label;\\n\\n        // Process points in batches of 4 using NEON SIMD\\n        int j = 0;\\n        for (; j + 3 < len; j += 4) {\\n            // Prefetch next cache lines to reduce latency\\n            __builtin_prefetch(xs + j + 8, 0, 1);\\n            __builtin_prefetch(ys + j + 8, 0, 1);\\n\\n            float32x4_t x_vec = vld1q_f32(xs + j);\\n            float32x4_t y_vec = vld1q_f32(ys + j);\\n\\n            float32x4_t dx = vsubq_f32(x_vec, tx_vec);\\n            float32x4_t dy = vsubq_f32(y_vec, ty_vec);\\n            // dist_sq = dx*dx + dy*dy\\n            float32x4_t dist_sq = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx, dx), dy, dy);\\n\\n            float d[4];\\n            vst1q_f32(d, dist_sq);\\n\\n            for (int t = 0; t < 4; t++) {\\n                heap_insert_or_replace(d[t], label, heap, &heap_size, k);\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Remainder scalar loop\\n        for (; j < len; j++) {\\n            Point p;\\n            p.x = xs[j];\\n            p.y = ys[j];\\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, p);\\n            heap_insert_or_replace(d, label, heap, &heap_size, k);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Copy labels from heap into labels array\\n    for (int i = 0; i < heap_size && i < k; i++) {\\n        labels[i] = heap[i+1].label;\\n    }\\n\\n    free(heap);\\n\\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\\n\\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\\n    int current_frequency = 1;\\n\\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n            }\\n            current_frequency = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            current_frequency++;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    free(labels);\\n    return most_frequent;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\\n    \\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\\n    }\\n\\n    int k = parse_k();\\n\\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\\n\\n    printf(\\\"%c\\\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float x;\\n    float y;\\n} Point;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    char label;\\n    int length;\\n    float *xs;\\n    float *ys;\\n} Group;\\n\\nvoid on_error() {\\n    printf(\\\"Invalid input file.\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\\n    int n;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" n_groups=%d \\\", &n) != 1) on_error();\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nPoint parse_point() {\\n    float x, y;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" (%f ,%f) \\\", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\\n    Point point;\\n    point.x = x;\\n    point.y = y;\\n    return point;\\n}\\n\\nGroup parse_next_group() {\\n    char label; \\n    int length;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" label=%c \\\", &label) != 1) on_error();\\n    if (scanf(\\\" length=%d \\\", &length) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    Group group;\\n    group.label = label;\\n    group.length = length;\\n    // Allocate with 16-byte alignment for efficient NEON loads\\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)&group.xs, 16, sizeof(float) * length)) {\\n        on_error();\\n    }\\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)&group.ys, 16, sizeof(float) * length)) {\\n        on_error();\\n    }\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        Point p = parse_point();\\n        group.xs[i] = p.x;\\n        group.ys[i] = p.y;\\n    }\\n\\n    return group;\\n}\\n\\nint parse_k() {\\n    int k;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" k=%d \\\", &k) != 1) on_error();\\n    return k;\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline float euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * (b.x - a.x)) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\\n}\\n\\nint compare_for_sort(const void *a, const void *b) {\\n  return *(char*)a - *(char*)b;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/knn.h\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Combining aligned allocation (posix_memalign to 16 bytes), hoisting NEON vector constants outside all loops, adding restrict qualifiers with __builtin_assume_aligned hints inside knn, prefetching upcoming cache lines in the batch loop, and using bit shifts for heap index calculations further reduces memory latency and instruction count while preserving legal SIMD/vectorization. These changes improve runtime over the SoA+NEON implementation.\",\n  \"notes\": \"All transformations are safe: alignment does not change semantics; hoisting constants is valid because to_evaluate is constant per call; restrict and assume_aligned help compiler generate better code without affecting correctness; prefetching is a hint; bit shifts produce same results as division for positive indices. The remainder scalar loop remains unchanged.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"posix_memalign for 16-byte alignment of coordinate arrays\",\n    \"hoist NEON vector constants (tx_vec, ty_vec) outside the outer group loop\",\n    \"add restrict qualifiers and __builtin_assume_aligned hints inside knn\",\n    \"prefetch upcoming cache lines in batch loop using __builtin_prefetch\",\n    \"use bit shifts for heap index calculations\"\n  ]\n}",
    "thinking": "We are role B with goal \"legal SIMD/vectorization and loop dependencies\". The current source is the SoA+NEON implementation from parent experiment 74722b26180e4b94. We have a history of experiments, many valid around ~0.03 seconds (score ~0.986). Baseline was ~2.09s. Our recent own role experiments: 6fbf23832e3a449b (alignment+hoisting+restrict), f208cc332ca8480c (hoist NEON constants + bit shifts), 6f7a258f9ca5447b (alignment+hoisting+restrict). All valid with similar times ~0.03s.\n\nWe need to propose a new transformation that improves SIMD/vectorization and loop dependencies further, while preserving correctness. The current code uses NEON intrinsics for batches of 4 points. We can consider:\n\n- Prefetching: add __builtin_prefetch for upcoming cache lines in the group loop.\n- Loop unrolling: manually unroll the inner batch loop to reduce overhead? But it's already processing 4 at a time; we could process 8 or use wider NEON (but ARM64 has 128-bit, so 4 floats). Could do two batches per iteration with prefetching.\n- Use vld1q_f32_x2 for loading interleaved xs and ys? But they are separate arrays. We can load both at once using vld2q_f32 if we had interleaved storage; but SoA is already good.\n- Reduce heap insertion overhead: the heap_insert_or_replace function is called per point (4 times per batch). Could inline it or use a faster approach? But previous experiments tried bit shifts etc. We could try to reduce branches in heap operations by using predicated moves? Not easy in C without intrinsics.\n\nAnother idea: Use NEON for the remainder scalar loop as well, but that's minor.\n\nMaybe we can hoist the vdupq_n_f32(tx) and ty outside the inner j loop entirely (they are invariant per group). Currently they are inside the batch loop. That was done in previous experiments? In current code, tx and ty are computed each iteration of the for-j loop. We should move them before the loop.\n\nAlso we can add restrict qualifiers to pointers in knn function: float *restrict xs, etc., and use __builtin_assume_aligned if we align allocations. But previous experiments did alignment? The parent experiment (74722b26180e4b94) likely didn't have alignment; later ones added posix_memalign but that might be in parse_next_group. In current source, group.xs/ys are allocated with malloc, not aligned. We can change to posix_memalign for 16-byte alignment (since NEON loads require only natural alignment? Actually vld1q_f32 requires 4-byte alignment; but better alignment helps). However we must be careful: changing allocation may affect correctness if the rest of code assumes malloc behavior, but it's fine.\n\nAlso add restrict to function parameters and local pointers.\n\nWe can also try to use __builtin_assume_aligned after posix_memalign.\n\nAnother idea: Use NEON for the heap insertion? Not straightforward.\n\nGiven that times are already very low (~0.03s), improvements may be marginal. But we need to propose something plausible.\n\nLet's design a transformation:\n\n1. In parse_next_group, use posix_memalign(&ptr, 16, sizeof(float)*length) instead of malloc for xs and ys.\n2. In knn function, add restrict qualifiers: float *restrict xs = g.xs; etc., and also heap pointer restrict? Not necessary.\n3. Hoist the vdupq_n_f32(tx) and ty outside the inner j loop (they are invariant per group). Actually tx and ty are constant for entire knn call, so we can compute them once before all groups. But to_evaluate is fixed; we can create float32x4_t tx_vec = vdupq_n_f32(to_evaluate.x); etc., outside the outer i loop.\n4. Prefetch: add __builtin_prefetch(xs + j + 8, 0, 1) and similarly for ys to bring in future cache lines.\n\n5. Use bit shifts for heap index calculations (already done? In current code they use idx/2; we can change to idx >>= 1). Also left = idx << 1; right = (idx << 1) + 1; but that's minor.\n\n6. Possibly unroll the inner batch loop by processing 8 points per iteration using two sets of NEON loads? But then remainder handling becomes more complex. Not sure if beneficial.\n\nGiven previous experiments, many have similar times. We need to propose something new. Let's check recent own role history: last valid experiment was 6f7a258f9ca5447b (alignment+hoisting+restrict) with score 0.985903 and time 0.02994s. That is slightly better than parent? Parent had 0.02981s. So alignment etc gave slight improvement.\n\nWe can try to combine all previous improvements: posix_memalign, restrict, hoist NEON constants outside loops, prefetching, bit shifts for heap indices. Also maybe use __builtin_assume_aligned after allocation and in knn with casts.\n\nAlso we could change the remainder scalar loop to also use NEON if len%4 !=0? But that's fine.\n\nAnother idea: Use vld1q_f32_x2 (if available) to load two consecutive vectors? Not needed.\n\nWe should ensure correctness. The changes are safe.\n\nLet's write new src/knn.c and src/knn.h with these transformations.\n\nIn knn.h, we need to modify parse_next_group to use posix_memalign. Also add restrict qualifiers in function signatures? But the header is used by other files; adding restrict may not affect correctness but could help compiler. We'll add restrict to parameters of euclidean_distance_no_sqrt and compare_for_sort? Not needed.\n\nIn knn.c, we need to include <stdint.h> for posix_memalign? Actually it's in stdlib.h already. But posix_memalign is POSIX; on Linux it works. We'll use #include <stdlib.h> (already). Also add __builtin_prefetch.\n\nWe must preserve the existing functionality: all sizes, seeds, repeated calls correct.\n\nLet's produce final files.\n\nAlso note sources_kept should be [] because integration_source_ids is empty.\n\nTransformations list: \"posix_memalign for 16-byte alignment\", \"hoist NEON vector constants outside loops\", \"add restrict qualifiers and __builtin_assume_aligned hints\", \"prefetch upcoming cache lines in batch loop\", \"use bit shifts for heap index calculations\".\n\nHypothesis: Combining aligned a